elated Medical group for that purpose; Demon and Monster Lore is Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+5. || HAND TO HAND: Aikido; Jujitsu or Karate for one other skill. || RELATED: six, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. Espionage''s Escape is Escape Artist. Mechanical''s Automotive is Automotive Mechanics. Military: None unless a member of the Bomb Squad (+10%): not offered, stated in the related note for the game master. || SECONDARY: three at each of levels one, four and ten, from the same list without bonuses; the book says select three at levels one, four and ten, read as three per level as the other Japan drafts read this sentence. || MONEY: one month''s salary, 2600 credits; no free room and board. || EQUIPMENT: AT-20 Sharpshooter is the AT-20 Sharpshot Police Special row. AT-23 stun rifle and/or AT-88 combat rifle is a choice of one, with the and/or in the note. Light body armor (typically Kuru or Trooper) is a choice of the AT-A11 and AT-A14 rows. The police radio is the walkie-talkie row. The police cruiser is a vehicle, not gear, and is prose in side_effects; jet packs and power armor are situational. || CYBERNETICS: 1D4+2 implants of choice at first level. The count is rolled, and an equipment choice takes a fixed count, so the implants are a prose ability rather than an equipment choice. || The book''s Note that 10% of the force are full conversion borgs, 12% partial borgs and 22% SAMAS pilots is in GM Notes; those officers are the Cyborg and SAMAS Samurai Pilot O.C.C.s."
