## Lore

The police of the Republic of Japan keep order in some of the most crowded and dangerous cities on Rifts Earth. Beyond the ordinary crime of any large city, a post-Rifts officer faces cyberoid street gangs, corporate ninja and tech-ninja, juicers, smugglers and drug dealers, supernatural predators hiding among the skyscrapers and sewers, the threat of demon-led raids, and riots stirred up by anti-techies, pro-techies, anti-D-bee groups, D-bee rights activists and many others. Through all of it they are expected to stay civil and courteous, and unlike soldiers they cannot reach for lethal force freely.

Every urban center has a large police department with its own jail, offices and science labs, where weapons, armor, vehicles and equipment are kept for the officers. The police keep the peace, make arrests, investigate crimes, root out supernatural predators and inhuman troublemakers, and help defend the city against invasion, working closely with the military. Both use special investigators, psychics, magic practitioners, and plain-clothes and uniformed officers. Police and military SAMAS patrol the skies above.

Officers get paramilitary training so they can support the Republican Army in an emergency. They know computers, cybernetics and technology well, carry a number of implants that aid their police work, and are trained to recognize the more common monsters and demons of Japan and how to fight them.

The police are respected and honored in the Republic, if slightly less so than the military, and most citizens cooperate with them fully; in turn, officers treat the public with respect and compassion. Most officers are honest and dedicated, but many feel beholden to the powerful corporations that influence the Republic, and are reluctant to pursue a case that might implicate one unless the evidence is overwhelming.

## GM Notes

When the evidence against a corporation is overwhelming, about 80% of officers will do their duty regardless of consequences. About 10% are in the corporations'' pockets, and some of those are deliberate plants (ninja or spies) who will inform the corporation and cover up evidence. The other 10% may feel honor-bound to warn the corporation first, giving its executives a chance to clear themselves or surrender honorably. Some 15% will take bribes to overlook petty or harmless crimes, including possession of illegal cybernetics, but 95% will not be bribed or intimidated away from serious crimes such as murder, rape or kidnapping. The chapter''s overview (printed 75) puts the force''s overall corruption at about 13%.

About 10% of the police force are full conversion borgs and another 12% are partially reconstructed borgs (see the Cyborg O.C.C.); 22% of the force are SAMAS pilots (see the SAMAS Samurai Pilot O.C.C.).

Officers who belong to the Bomb Squad may take Military skills (+10%) as O.C.C. Related skills; the class does not offer Military by default.
